T*
(   1. Mail User Agent \(MUA\): The end-user client interface \(e.g., Outlook, Apple Mail,) Tj
T*
(   Thunderbird, or Webmail\) used to compose, send, and read emails.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mail Transfer Agent \(MTA\): Server software \(e.g., Postfix, Sendmail, Exim\) responsible for) Tj
T*
(   routing and forwarding emails across the Internet using SMTP.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mail Delivery Agent \(MDA\): Software \(e.g., Dovecot\) that accepts incoming emails from the) Tj
T*
(   receiving MTA and deposits them into the recipient user's local mailbox storage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Protocol Workflow:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Sender composes email in MUA and transmits it to Sender's MTA via SMTP \(Port 587 with) Tj
T*
(   STARTTLS authentication\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Sender's MTA queries DNS for the MX records of the recipient's domain.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Sender's MTA establishes an SMTP connection to Recipient's MTA over Port 25 and) Tj
T*
(   transfers the message.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Recipient's MTA hands the email to the local MDA.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Recipient's MUA retrieves mail from the mailbox server using either POP3 \(Port 110/995,) Tj
T*
(   downloading and deleting locally\) or IMAP \(Port 143/993, maintaining synchronized folder states) Tj
T*
(   on the server\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
