(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Simple Network Management Protocol \(SNMP\) architecture, explaining Managers, Agents, MIBs, and SMI.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   SNMP is an application-layer framework used to monitor, configure, and manage networked devices) Tj
T*
(   \(routers, switches, firewalls, servers\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Core Architectural Components:) Tj
T*
(   1. SNMP Manager \(NMS\): The centralized management station that monitors network health, issues) Tj
T*
(   query requests, and receives alerts.) Tj
T*
(   2. SNMP Agent: Software running locally on managed network devices that gathers local) Tj
T*
(   operational metrics and executes configuration changes.) Tj
T*
(   3. Management Information Base \(MIB\): A structured, hierarchical virtual database maintained by) Tj
T*
(   the agent containing operational parameters \(e.g., interface packet counters, CPU usage, link) Tj
T*
(   status\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Structure of Management Information \(SMI\): Specifies the data definition rules and Abstract) Tj
T*
(   Syntax Notation One \(ASN.1\) data types used to define MIB objects.) Tj
T*
(   5. Object Identifiers \(OIDs\): Hierarchical dotted numeric strings \(e.g., 1.3.6.1.2.1.1.1 for) Tj
T*
(   sysDescr\) uniquely identifying variables in the MIB tree.) Tj
T*
(   6. Operational Operations: GetRequest, GetNextRequest, GetBulkRequest, SetRequest) Tj
T*
(   \(configuration write\), and Trap/Inform \(unsolicited asynchronous alerts sent by agents upon) Tj
T*
(   alarms\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
