(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the CIA Triad of Computer Security and detail complementary security principles: Non-Repudiation, Authenticity, and Authorization.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Information security frameworks are built upon foundational guarantees:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The CIA Triad:) Tj
T*
(   1. Confidentiality: Ensuring sensitive data is shielded from unauthorized observation or) Tj
T*
(   disclosure, implemented via strong encryption \(AES, RSA\) and access controls.) Tj
T*
(   2. Integrity: Guaranteeing that data has not been altered, tampered with, or corrupted in) Tj
T*
(   transit or storage, verified via cryptographic hashes \(SHA-256\) and message authentication) Tj
T*
(   codes \(HMAC\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Availability: Ensuring authorized users have uninterrupted, timely access to network) Tj
T*
(   services and information assets, protected via redundancy, DDoS mitigations, and failover) Tj
T*
(   architectures.) Tj
T*
