T*
(   Security Foundation: An attacker knows \(e, n\). Finding d requires calculating phi\(n\) =) Tj
T*
(   \(p-1\)\(q-1\), which requires factoring n into p and q. For 2048-bit keys, factoring n is) Tj
T*
(   computationally infeasible on classical computers.) Tj
