(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the complete Transport Layer Security \(TLS 1.3\) handshake protocol, detailing 1-RTT and 0-RTT connection establishment.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   TLS 1.3 \(RFC 8446\) streamlines handshake latency, mandates perfect forward secrecy, and) Tj
T*
(   eliminates insecure legacy ciphers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1-RTT Full Handshake:) Tj
T*
(   1. ClientHello \(Client -> Server\): Client sends supported cipher suites, random nonce, and) Tj
T*
(   speculatively sends its Ephemeral Diffie-Hellman key share \(KeyShare\).) Tj
T*
(   2. ServerHello \(Server -> Client\): Server selects the cipher suite, sends its own DH key share) Tj
T*
(   \(KeyShare\), and both immediately compute the shared session encryption key.) Tj
T*
(   3. Encrypted Extensions, Certificate, and CertificateVerify \(Server -> Client\): Sent ENCRYPTED) Tj
T*
(   using the newly computed session key. Server includes its X.509 certificate and a digital) Tj
T*
(   signature over handshake transcript.) Tj
T*
(   4. Finished \(Server -> Client\): HMAC over entire handshake transcript.) Tj
T*
(   5. Finished & HTTP Data \(Client -> Server\): Client verifies server signature, returns Finished,) Tj
T*
(   and begins streaming encrypted application HTTP data within 1 RTT!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   0-RTT Resumption \(Early Data\):) Tj
T*
(   Clients connecting to a previously visited server can send encrypted application data in the) Tj
T*
(   very first packet \(ClientHello\) using a pre-shared key \(PSK\) derived from the prior session.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 17:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Categorize network Firewalls by architecture: Packet-Filtering, Stateful Inspection, Application-Level Proxy, and Next-Generation Firewalls \(NGFW\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Firewalls enforce access control policies between distinct security zones across network) Tj
T*
(   layers:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Stateless Packet-Filtering Firewalls \(Layer 3/4\):) Tj
T*
(   - Inspects individual packet headers in isolation \(Source/Dest IP, Source/Dest Port, Protocol\).) Tj
T*
(   - High speed and low latency, but cannot track connection state or detect multi-packet payload) Tj
T*
(   exploits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Stateful Inspection Firewalls \(Layer 3/4\):) Tj
T*
(   - Maintains a Dynamic State Table tracking active connections \(SYN, ESTABLISHED, FIN\).) Tj
T*
(   - Automatically permits returning inbound traffic belonging to an established outbound session) Tj
T*
(   without requiring open incoming ports.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Application-Level Proxy Firewalls \(Layer 7\):) Tj
T*
(   - Terminates connection from client, parses and inspects complete application layer protocols) Tj
T*
(   \(HTTP, FTP\), and initiates a separate connection to target server.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
