(   [Problem Statement]: Describe Post-Quantum Cryptography \(PQC\), explaining why Shor's and Grover's quantum algorithms threaten classical cryptography and highlighting NIST standards.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Quantum computing utilizes quantum superposition and entanglement to solve specific) Tj
T*
(   mathematical problems in exponential time:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Quantum Threats to Classical Ciphers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Shor's Algorithm: Can compute prime factorization and discrete logarithms in polynomial) Tj
T*
(   time. Once large fault-tolerant quantum computers exist, Shor's algorithm will instantly break) Tj
T*
(   RSA, Diffie-Hellman, DSA, and Elliptic Curve Cryptography \(ECC\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Grover's Algorithm: Provides quadratic speedup for unstructured database searches,) Tj
T*
(   effectively halving the brute-force security of symmetric ciphers. Mitigation: Doubling AES key) Tj
T*
(   sizes from 128 to 256 bits maintains 128 bits of quantum security.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   NIST Post-Quantum Cryptography \(PQC\) Standards:) Tj
T*
(   NIST standardized quantum-resistant algorithms based on mathematical problems that quantum) Tj
T*
(   computers cannot solve efficiently:) Tj
T*
(   - Key Encapsulation \(General Encryption\): ML-KEM \(CRYSTALS-Kyber\), based on Module Learning) Tj
T*
(   with Errors over lattices.) Tj
T*
(   - Digital Signatures: ML-DSA \(CRYSTALS-Dilithium\) and SLH-DSA \(SPHINCS+, stateless hash-based) Tj
T*
(   signatures\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
