/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Calculate an RSA signature and verification manually for small prime parameters: p=5, q=11, message hash h=9, and encryption exponent e=3.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   RSA Digital Signature Walkthrough:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Modulus and Totient Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   - n = p * q = 5 * 11 = 55.) Tj
T*
(   - phi\(n\) = \(p - 1\) * \(q - 1\) = 4 * 10 = 40.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Private Exponent \(d\):) Tj
T*
(   - Must satisfy: \(d * e\) mod phi\(n\) = 1 -> \(d * 3\) mod 40 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - We find d such that 3d = 40k + 1. For k=2: 3d = 81 -> d = 27.) Tj
T*
(   - Public Key: \(e=3, n=55\); Private Key: \(d=27, n=55\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Signing Message Hash \(h = 9\):) Tj
T*
(   - Signature S = \(h^d\) mod n = 9^27 mod 55.) Tj
T*
(   - By modular exponentiation: 9^1 = 9, 9^2 = 81 = 26 mod 55, 9^3 = 26 * 9 = 234 = 14 mod 55.) Tj
T*
(   - Continuing calculations yields Signature S = 14 mod 55.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Verifying Signature \(S = 14\):) Tj
T*
(   - Recipient computes: h' = \(S^e\) mod n = 14^3 mod 55.) Tj
T*
