(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the functionality and deployment of Honeypots, Honeynets, and Intrusion Detection/Prevention Systems \(IDS/IPS\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Proactive cybersecurity relies on layered detection and deception architectures:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Honeypots & Honeynets:) Tj
T*
(   - A Honeypot is an intentionally exposed, closely monitored decoy server containing synthetic) Tj
T*
(   data designed to lure attackers.) Tj
T*
(   - Low-Interaction Honeypot: Emulates specific network services \(e.g., fake SSH or HTTP daemons\)) Tj
T*
(   to collect attack trends and IP lists.) Tj
T*
(   - High-Interaction Honeypot: Runs full real operating systems in isolated virtualization to) Tj
T*
(   study sophisticated Zero-Day malware behavior and rootkit techniques.) Tj
T*
(   - Honeynet: A coordinated network of multiple honeypots simulating an enterprise intranet.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. IDS vs IPS Deployment:) Tj
T*
(   - Intrusion Detection System \(IDS\): Deployed out-of-band via switch SPAN/mirror ports.) Tj
T*
(   Passively inspects traffic copies and generates alerts without impacting network throughput.) Tj
T*
(   - Intrusion Prevention System \(IPS\): Deployed directly inline between switches/firewalls.) Tj
T*
(   Analyzes traffic in real-time and actively drops malicious packets or resets connections.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 28:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structure and operation of Secure Sockets Layer / Transport Layer Security record protocols and cipher suites.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   TLS is divided into two primary operational sub-layers: Handshake Protocol and Record Protocol:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. TLS Record Protocol \(Lower Layer\):) Tj
T*
(   - Fragments outgoing application data into blocks <= 16 KB.) Tj
T*
(   - Applies cryptographic Message Authentication Code \(MAC\) or Authenticated Encryption with) Tj
T*
(   Associated Data \(AEAD\) like AES-GCM.) Tj
T*
(   - Encrypts payload and prepends a 5-byte TLS Record Header \(Content Type, Protocol Version,) Tj
T*
(   Length\).) Tj
T*
(   - Transmits record across underlying TCP socket.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Anatomy of a Standard TLS 1.2 Cipher Suite String:) Tj
T*
(   Example: TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256) Tj
T*
(   - Key Exchange: ECDHE \(Ephemeral Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman for Perfect Forward Secrecy\).) Tj
T*
(   - Authentication: RSA digital certificates.) Tj
T*
(   - Bulk Encryption: AES with 128-bit key in GCM mode.) Tj
T*
(   - PRF / Hash: SHA-256 for pseudo-random key generation.) Tj
T*
(   In TLS 1.3, this is streamlined to TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 \(key exchange and auth are negotiated) Tj
T*
(   independently\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
